this_file: NOTICE

The Kerning category adapts five Apache-2.0 fontlab-samples scripts retained in
fontlab-python-examples/_old/part4/fontlab-samples/samples/:
kerning_classes_browser.py, kerning_compare_masters.py, kerning_list_browser.py,
kerning_missing_pairs.py and kerning_text_preview.py. Source and destination
SHA-256 mappings are recorded in migration.json. Native access and shared
lifecycle adaptations live in fontlab-fontlabapp (see its NOTICE). Every original
control is retained; error containment and complete-ink proof fitting are added.
See LICENSE for the Apache License, Version 2.0. Original sources stay unchanged.

Five additional Kerning editors adapt these Apache-2.0 sources from the same
retained samples directory: kerning_copy_between_masters.py,
kerning_pair_editor.py, kerning_scale_values.py, kerning_round_values.py and
kerning_remove_small.py. All controls/actions and original interfaces are
retained. Shared calculations, multi-master preflight/writing and common UI
rendering now live in App. Snapshot refusal, explicit-zero insertion and Refresh
recovery are added. The five original source/destination hashes are appended to
migration.json without changing prior mappings. Native acceptance is pending.

Selected Kerning editors adapt Apache-2.0 kerning_exceptions_finder.py and
kerning_pairs_from_text.py from the same retained fontlab-samples archive.
App's kerning_selection.py shares exception precedence, word parsing, explicit/
effective previews and ticked plans; the existing complete batch writer and
owned dialog shell provide snapshot guards, Refresh and history. Scriptmix
migration.json appends both source/destination hashes; originals are unchanged.
